Restore the child layout margin in the Qt 6 style

Commit fbadbbf3 ("copy qt5 to qt6") copied qt5/ to qt6/. Commit a501c957
and commit 23e2ad04 then deleted the cases for the three metrics that
Qt 6 no longer defines. The four layout margin cases now return 9 pixels
for every widget, and layoutSpacing returns 4 pixels. The Qt 5 style
returns 9 pixels for a window and 6 pixels for a child layout. It returns
2 pixels when OpenOffice asks without a widget. Its layout spacing is
6 pixels.

Dolphin 26.08 sets the height of the StatusBarSpaceInfo widget in
src/statusbar/dolphinstatusbar.cpp. Line 126 takes the greatest of the
font height, the minimum zoom slider height, and the stop button height.
Dolphin hides that button at line 97, and adds it to the layout at line
149. The button therefore keeps the default geometry of a child widget,
which is 30 pixels high. With a 10 point font the other two values are
16 and 23 pixels. Line 135 then makes 30 pixels the fixed height of the
space widget.

Line 39 of src/statusbar/statusbarspaceinfo.cpp passes -1 for the top and
the bottom margin of the layout, so the style sets both. A 9 pixel margin
leaves 12 pixels for the contents. The free space bar asks for the
greater of the font height and its 12 pixel bar. A 16 pixel font
therefore costs the bar 4 pixels of height. The button beside the bar
holds the free space text, and cuts it at the top and at the bottom.

Restore the Qt 5 values. A window keeps the 9 pixel margin. The space
widget gets a 6 pixel margin, and 18 pixels for its contents. A layout
that sets no spacing again leaves 6 pixels between its widgets. Breeze
gives the same 18 pixels and the same 6 pixel gap.

The change sits on the branch work/child-layout-margin of the local tree. The
fork wyn/qtcurve holds that branch. Merge request !7 on system/qtcurve holds
that branch as the source.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/style/qtcurve.cpp b/qt6/style/qtcurve.cpp
index 2cf76a44..7ec26c1b 100644
--- a/qt6/style/qtcurve.cpp
+++ b/qt6/style/qtcurve.cpp
@@ -1164,7 +1164,8 @@ int Style::layoutSpacing(QSizePolicy::ControlType control1,
     Q_UNUSED(orientation);
     Q_UNUSED(option);
     Q_UNUSED(widget);
-    return 4;
+    // Qt 6 has no PM_DefaultLayoutSpacing. Keep the Qt 5 value of 6 pixels.
+    return 6;
 }
 
 // Use 'drawItemTextWithRole' when already know which role to use.
diff --git a/qt6/style/qtcurve_api.cpp b/qt6/style/qtcurve_api.cpp
index 0d3a2fb7..faf4880f 100644
--- a/qt6/style/qtcurve_api.cpp
+++ b/qt6/style/qtcurve_api.cpp
@@ -1589,7 +1589,13 @@ Style::pixelMetric(PixelMetric metric, const QStyleOption *option,
     case PM_LayoutTopMargin:
     case PM_LayoutRightMargin:
     case PM_LayoutBottomMargin:
-        return 9;
+        // Qt 6 has no PM_DefaultTopLevelMargin and no PM_DefaultChildMargin.
+        // Keep the Qt 5 values. A window gets 9 pixels. Any other layout
+        // gets 6 pixels, or 2 pixels when OpenOffice asks without a widget.
+        if ((option && (option->state & State_Window)) ||
+            (widget && widget->isWindow()))
+            return 9;
+        return isOOWidget(widget) ? 2 : 6;
     case PM_MenuBarItemSpacing:
         return 0;
     case PM_ToolBarItemMargin:
